    <h2 style="margin:52px 0 16px;color:#181818;font-size:34px;line-height:1.12;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-1.15px;">
        Proven ingredients that help fade stubborn pigment
    </h2>
    <p style="margin:0 0 22px;">
        Fading dark marks comes down to combining a few proven cosmetic ingredients that target pigment at different stages:
    </p>

    <ul style="margin:0 0 22px;padding-left:22px;">
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Tyrosinase inhibitors.</strong> Kojic acid slows down tyrosinase, the main enzyme that makes melanin. This reduces new pigment production at the source.<sup><a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/42654049/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" style="color:#B87330;text-decoration:none;">[4]</a></sup>
</li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Melanosome transfer blockers.</strong> Niacinamide (vitamin B3) prevents pigment packages from moving into surface skin cells, keeping excess colour from showing up as dark patches.<sup><a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/12100180/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" style="color:#B87330;text-decoration:none;">[5]</a></sup>
</li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Gentle renewal agents.</strong> Bio-retinoids encourage surface cells to shed at a normal rate, bringing fresh, evenly toned cells to the surface without provoking peeling or sun sensitivity.<sup><a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34751927/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" style="color:#B87330;text-decoration:none;">[6]</a></sup>
</li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Barrier-supporting lipids.</strong> Ceramides and cholesterol keep the skin hydrated and comfortable so active ingredients do not cause stinging or flaking.</li>
    </ul>

    <p style="margin:0 0 22px;">
        Using one serum that combines these ingredients is gentler than layering four separate bottles. A formula like <a href="/products/dark-spots-pore-control-serum-30ml" style="color:#181818;text-decoration-color:#B87330;text-decoration-thickness:2px;text-underline-offset:4px;">Dark Spots, Pore Control Serum</a> pairs kojic acid, niacinamide, bio-retinoids, six peptides, and five ceramides to address marks and barrier resilience in one step.
    </p>

    
    <div style="margin:34px 0;padding:24px 26px;border-top:1px solid #B87330;border-bottom:1px solid #B87330;background:#FFFEF3;">
        <p style="margin:0 0 7px;color:#B87330;font-size:12px;line-height:1.2;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;">Keep in mind</p>
        <p style="margin:0;color:#181818;">
            Fading dark marks takes patience. Natural surface cell turnover takes roughly 28 to 40 days, so expect visible lightening between four and eight weeks. Skipping sunscreen for even one sunny afternoon can trigger pigment cells and undo weeks of steady progress.
        </p>
    </div>

    <h2 style="margin:52px 0 16px;color:#181818;font-size:34px;line-height:1.12;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-1.15px;">
        A simple daily routine for post-acne marks
    </h2>
    <p style="margin:0 0 22px;">
        A simple routine prevents irritation and is easy to follow every day:
    </p>

    <ol style="margin:0 0 22px;padding-left:24px;">
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Gentle cleansing (Morning and Evening).</strong> Wash with a mild cleanser that removes oil without leaving skin tight. Skip physical scrubs, which irritate the surface.</li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Targeted serum (Morning and Evening).</strong> Smooth three to four drops of serum over clean, damp skin across your whole face, not just on individual spots.</li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Moisturiser (Morning and Evening).</strong> Apply a light moisturiser with ceramides or squalane to lock in hydration.</li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Sunscreen (Every Morning).</strong> Finish with broad-spectrum SPF 50 and PA++++ protection. Reapply if outdoors.</li>
    </ol>

    <p style="margin:0 0 22px;">
        If you use <a href="/products/dark-spots-pore-control-serum-30ml" style="color:#181818;text-decoration-color:#B87330;text-decoration-thickness:2px;text-underline-offset:4px;">Dark Spots, Pore Control Serum</a>, it acts as your sole active morning and night. In the serum's clinical study on 36 Indian women aged 24 to 44 with twice-daily use, 100% of participants improved dark spots at eight weeks. The study recorded melanin down 32.8% and visible pore area down 19.3% at four weeks, with hydration up 254% at two weeks and collagen up 132.4% at eight weeks. Results may vary.
    </p>

    <h2 style="margin:52px 0 16px;color:#181818;font-size:34px;line-height:1.12;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-1.15px;">
        Comparing approaches for post-acne skin
    </h2>
    <div style="margin:24px 0 34px;overflow-x:auto;border-top:2px solid #181818;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(24,24,24,.25);">
        <table style="width:100%;min-width:620px;border-collapse:collapse;text-align:left;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;">
            <thead>
                <tr style="background:#FFFEF3;">
