    <h2 style="margin:52px 0 16px;color:#181818;font-size:34px;line-height:1.12;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-1.15px;">
        Why daily sunscreen is non-negotiable
    </h2>
    <p style="margin:0 0 22px;">
        Brightening serums cannot work if you skip sunscreen. Ultraviolet light, especially UVA rays, directly stimulates pigment cells to produce melanin. On healing post-acne skin, these cells are hypersensitive and react to even brief sun exposure by darkening the mark.
    </p>

    <p style="margin:0 0 22px;">
        Recent research shows that visible light, especially blue light from the sun, also causes long-lasting pigmentation in darker skin tones.<sup><a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/42793277/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" style="color:#B87330;text-decoration:none;">[7]</a></sup> In sunny climates across India, daily broad-spectrum sunscreen is essential even if you stay indoors near windows. Choose a lightweight gel or fluid that leaves no white cast, apply two finger-lengths every morning, and reapply before afternoon sun.
    </p>

    <h2 style="margin:52px 0 16px;color:#181818;font-size:34px;line-height:1.12;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-1.15px;">
        Realistic timelines: what to expect week by week
    </h2>
    <p style="margin:0 0 22px;">
        Skin renews itself gradually, so progress happens in distinct stages over several weeks:
    </p>

    <ul style="margin:0 0 22px;padding-left:22px;">
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Weeks 1 to 2:</strong> Skin feels more comfortable and hydrated. Redness around recovering pimples begins to calm down, though dark pigment looks unchanged.</li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Weeks 3 to 4:</strong> Skin texture feels smoother, pores look clearer, and the edges of dark spots start to soften.</li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Weeks 6 to 8:</strong> Superficial marks show noticeable fading, and your overall skin tone looks more even.</li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Weeks 8 to 12:</strong> Older, more stubborn marks show substantial lightening. Consistent sunscreen keeps new marks from forming.</li>
    </ul>

    
    <h2 style="margin:56px 0 18px;color:#181818;font-size:34px;line-height:1.12;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-1.15px;">
        Frequently asked questions
    </h2>
    <div style="border-top:2px solid #181818;">
        <div style="padding:22px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(24,24,24,.2);">
            <h3 style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#181818;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.25px;">How long do post-acne dark spots take to fade completely?</h3>
            <p style="margin:0;">Most surface dark spots take two to six months to fade with consistent care, while deeper marks take six to twelve months. Daily sunscreen and gentle pigment inhibitors prevent them from darkening as skin renews itself.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="padding:22px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(24,24,24,.2);">
            <h3 style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#181818;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.25px;">What is the difference between a dark spot and an acne scar?</h3>
            <p style="margin:0;">A dark spot is flat and caused by excess melanin, leaving skin texture smooth. A true acne scar damages collagen, creating indented pits or raised tissue that you can feel with your fingertips.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="padding:22px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(24,24,24,.2);">
            <h3 style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#181818;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.25px;">Can I use vitamin C and niacinamide together for dark spots?</h3>
            <p style="margin:0;">Yes, vitamin C and niacinamide can be used together safely. They target dark spots through distinct pathways and improve overall tone without interfering with each other.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="padding:22px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(24,24,24,.2);">
            <h3 style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#181818;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.25px;">Does scrubbing my skin help dark spots fade faster?</h3>
            <p style="margin:0;">No, physical scrubs make dark spots worse. Scrubbing inflames the skin and triggers pigment cells to produce extra melanin, deepening discoloration. Gentle chemical renewal is far safer.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="padding:22px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(24,24,24,.2);">
            <h3 style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#181818;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.25px;">Should I treat active acne or dark spots first?</h3>
            <p style="margin:0;">Treat active acne first or address both together with non-irritating formulas. Fading marks while fresh pimples appear traps you in a cycle, as every new breakout produces another dark spot.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="padding:22px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(24,24,24,.2);">
            <h3 style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#181818;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.25px;">Why do my dark spots look darker after being in the sun for just one day?</h3>
            <p style="margin:0;">Ultraviolet and visible light trigger pigment cells to make melanin in self-defense. Skin healing from acne inflammation is especially sensitive, so even brief unprotected exposure causes rapid darkening.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="padding:22px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(24,24,24,.2);">
            <h3 style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#181818;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.25px;">Can I use brightening serums while pregnant or breastfeeding?</h3>
            <p style="margin:0;">It depends on the formula. While niacinamide and azelaic acid are widely considered suitable, salicylic acid and retinoids are generally avoided during pregnancy. Check the ingredient list with your doctor.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    
